3 STAE Ribnica
3 CTRY Slovenia
1 OCCU graščak, veleposestnik
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.slovenska-biografija.si/oseba/sbi523950/
2 CONT
2 CONT Google Translation:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudež Anton, auditor, lord r. April 8, 1757 in Kobja Glava on the Karst (parish of Štanjel), u. Nov 14 1829 in Ribnica. At the gymnast. v Lj. was at least 1769-73 a classmate of Guide, l. In 1777 he practiced at the account office
2 CONC  in Lj. From home he was known to the Counts of Kobencli (SBL I, 83, 476), who had estates up there. Karst (Štanjel, Lodges near Vipava, Predjama, Prosek) and in Ribnica na Dol., R. served in their service as a clerk of the fish f
2 CONC arm in 1789 and as a tenant in 1793. In 1798 he purchased the Stang gilts and the Mengeš and Dragomlje courts and laid the foundation for a large manor estate from year to year: he acquired 1801 Vič, 1803 Loko pri Mengšu, 30 July.
2 CONC  1810 bought from Count John Philip Kobenzel (SBL I, 476) the dominion of Ribnica with the incorporated estate Breg near Ribnica. In addition, R. also had a house in Lj. (No. 34, Stari trg) and since 1821 the Tolsti vrh estate (Gr
2 CONC acar's turn). Under his peasantry, the subjects were allowed to divide the land.
2 CONT
2 CONT R. comes from the first group of Lj. students who were attentive and sympathetic to the birth ideas of the Kumerde Plan (SBL I, 583) and Pohlin's work. Friendship with the Guide and close relationship with Zois not only solidified
2 CONC  this orientation but also gave her many initiatives. Zois himself maintained alliances with R in l. 1813–9, when he had already restricted his correspondence with others. As a friend of Zois, R. was able to meet and befriend Kopi
2 CONC tar at his house, who delivered him his son Joseph (see Art.) For a year in Vienna and allowed them both to travel around Germany. He remained with Kopitar in friendly relations until his death, even though he treated his father a
2 CONC nd son without embarrassment, as they deserved ”(Letter to Zois August 15, 1812). The guide, R's friend from a young age, was almost a daily guest of R's house during his time as a cooperator in Ribnica (1788-93). Jakob Zupan. Whe
2 CONC n the Guide went to Koprivnik, he not only informed Ra about his educational work, but also sent him a dictionary work for review, to which R. partly contributed consumables, partly reviewed the contributions of his colleagues (eg
2 CONC  Jarnik's). To the guide and his circle, he was a "congregatio slavicorum rituum", an advisor even in complicated language issues. He accumulated linguistic peculiarities, folk songs (especially for St. Vraz). The most beautiful b
2 CONC allads the Guide left in the manuscript are probably from the Ribnica Valley and R's collection. However, it seems that R. lost his keen interest in Slavic studies after his death. - Cf. NUK: Ms 446 c, 466, 467, 558; Glaser II, 38
2 CONC , 185, 209; Kidrič, Dobrovský 25, 58, 181; same, Story, Index; the same, ZKor 1939, 189; 1941, 108, 119; Fr. Levec, LZ 1889, 396; Iv. Superintendent, IMK 1899, 52; IP, Veda 1911, 386, 387; parish report. office Kobja glava, 4 aug.
2 CONC  1952; M. Smole, Kron 1956, 172–3. UM lost his keen interest in Slavic studies after his death. - Cf. NUK: Ms 446 c, 466, 467, 558; Glaser II, 38, 185, 209; Kidrič, Dobrovský 25, 58, 181; same, Story, Index; the same, ZKor 1939, 1
2 CONC 89; 1941, 108, 119; Fr. Levec, LZ 1889, 396; Iv. Superintendent, IMK 1899, 52; IP, Veda 1911, 386, 387; parish report. office Kobja glava, 4 aug. 1952; M. Smole, Kron 1956, 172–3. UM lost his keen interest in Slavic studies after 
2 CONC his death. - Cf. NUK: Ms 446 c, 466, 467, 558; Glaser II, 38, 185, 209; Kidrič, Dobrovský 25, 58, 181; same, Story, Index; the same, ZKor 1939, 189; 1941, 108, 119; Fr. Levec, LZ 1889, 396; Iv. Superintendent, IMK 1899, 52; IP, Ve
2 CONC da 1911, 386, 387; parish report. office Kobja glava, 4 aug. 1952; M. Smole, Kron 1956, 172–3. UM
2 CONT
2 CONT Milena Uršič
2 CONT
