1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sy was in die Norvalspont konsentrasiekamp saam met van haar kinders, insluitende Sarel Daniel Snyman.
2 CONT (She was in the British concentration camp in Norvalspont South Africa with her children, including Sarel Daniel Snyman.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Norvalspont Konsentrasiekamp databasis inligting hieronder blyk om haar profiel te pas:
2 CONT URL:  https://www2.lib.uct.ac.za/mss/bccd/CampsSearch/1/1/0/1/  
2 CONT Die databasis kan ook verkry word vanuit http://maroelamedia.co.za/konsentrasiekampe/
2 CONT
2 CONT Her initials seem to be recorded incorrectly as "I P"  in stead of "J M P". This can be explained as follow:  "J" looks similar to "I" in writing, the middle "M" was dropped and the last "P" was correct. 
2 CONT Her age according to geni (born 27 Feb 1856) should be 45 at arrival (21/04/1901) and 46 when departing (2/09/1902), but the camp records noted her as 47 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children noted below matches her Geni profile, so I do not think there is any uncertainty that this is her:
2 CONT
2 CONT "British Concentration Camps of the South African War [2nd Anglo-Boer war)1900-1902:
2 CONT Personal Details
2 CONT Name:	Mrs I P Snyman
2 CONT Born in camp?	No
2 CONT Died in camp?	No
2 CONT Gender:	female
2 CONT Race:	white
2 CONT Marital status:	married
2 CONT Nationality:	Free State
2 CONT Unique ID:	40515
2 CONT Camp History
2 CONT Name:	Norvals Pont RC
2 CONT Age arrival:	47
2 CONT Date arrival:	21/04/1901
2 CONT Date departure:	02/09/1902
2 CONT Destination:	Prior Station
2 CONT Farm History
2 CONT Name:	Vlakplaats
2 CONT District:	Bethulie
2 CONT Relationships
2 CONT Mrs I P Snyman is the wife of Mr P J Snyman
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT Title:	SRC 85 Norvals Pont CR
2 CONT Type:	Camp register
2 CONT Location:	Free State Archives Repository
2 CONT Reference No.:	85
2 CONT Notes:	p.4
2 CONT
2 CONT Acknowledgments: The project was funded by the Wellcome Trust, which is not responsible for the contents of the database. The help of the following research assistants is gratefully acknowledged: Ryna Boshoff, Murray Gorman, Janie
2 CONC  Grobler, Marelize Grobler, Luke Humby, Clare O’Reilly Jacomina Roose, Elsa Strydom, Mary van Blerk. Thanks also go to Peter Dennis for the design of the original database and to Dr Iain Smith, co-grantholder."
2 CONT Source: https://www2.lib.uct.ac.za/mss/bccd/CampsSearch/1/1/0/1/
2 CONT (Modified by Kornelius Snyman on 26 January 2022.)
