2 ADDR
3 CITY Graaff-Reinet
3 STAE Cape Colony
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gerrit Kruger was the great grandfather of Stephanus Johannes Paulus (Paul) Kruger born 10 October 1825. Paul Kruger was President of the South African Republic from 1883 to 1900. Gerrit Kruger was born 1750, He's 
2 CONC father was Hendrik Kruger born 1725. His parents were Casper Kruger and Elsie Steyn. In 1836 they joined the Potgieter trek. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerrit Kruger was ‘n boer in die Graaff-Reinet omgewing, Hy is op sy plaas oorlede, en daar is hy ook begrawe
2 CONT Plaas Rheboksfontein, Agter Zuurberg  , District  Graaff-Reinet 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Earlier lives of the Krugers extract ''' (c)2 Gerrit, b. 21.5.1750; md. (1) Susanna Lasya Buys on 12.10.1769, d. of Stephanus  Buijs and Maria Elisabeth de Vries; (2) on 15.5.1808 Anna Sophia Venter, widow of Phillip  Snyman (C
2 CONC O 2567, Matrimonial List G.R., Item No. 16). Marriage omitted in Geslacht  Register. Gerrit Kruger would have been about twelve when the family moved from Oliphants-  berg near the shores of Table Bay. No farm grant in the Roggeve
2 CONC ld has been traced to him and  though he married when about twenty he does not appear to have made an "opgaaf" (census  return) before 1772. In 1778 he is in the Stellenbosch Roll as owning only twenty horned cattle  (runderen) an
2 CONC d a hundred sheep. 11 
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of his bride, who died very shortly before Gerrit's marriage, was Stephanus Buijs,  a Roggeveld farmer who left an estate valued at Rds. 737. That the Buijs were neighbours of the  Krugers in the Roggeveld is shown by t
2 CONC he fact that the inventory of Stephanus Buys was made  by Gerrit's brother Johannes Jacob (c)l and their uncle Pieter Ernst (b)7 on 19.2. 1769 12 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1778, too-noticeably the year in which his father Hendrik (b)6 vacated de Plaat - Gerrit  was at the October Militia Exercise at Stellenbosch as a mounted man in the Company commanded by Capt. Phillipus Wouter de Vos. It is pro
2 CONC bable, however, that Gerrit, like his  father and brothers, was in Graaff Reinet before or during 1780, for though his farm  Leeuwenkuyl was only officially granted in 1785 it does not follow that he was not there some  years befo
2 CONC re the grant. Like other burghers known to have been in Graaff Reinet his census  return continues to be in the Stellenbosch Roll until 1787, when the Drostdy or Magistracy of  Graaff Reinet was established. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerrit Kruger's progress as farmer is reflected in the returns he made: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1777 wife, son, daughter and a horse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1785 family, two hundred sheep, twenty cattle, a horse, no slave or knegt. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1791 one thousand sheep, one hundred cattle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1804 nine hundred sheep, fifty hamels, six horses for breeding, three for saddle, three  hundred goats. For labour twelve Hottentot servants-male, female and children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He, at that time, was probably at Brandvlei and certainly in the Veldcornetcy of FC Willem  Sterrenberg Pretorius. With him was his wife, two of his sons and two daughters. He had some  years before 13 been "on the farm of the Hon
2 CONC . Nicolaas van der Walt". This was Grootfontein. In  1798, already called d'oude, he took a leading part in an act aimed at pacifying Bushmen. The  burghers of Agter Sneeuwberg joined in collecting cattle and sheep for presentatio
2 CONC n to such of  the savages as professed willingness to cease their raids and become pastoralists. On 18.11.1798  283 sheep, given by burghers, were collected at Grootfontein and on 17.12.1798 most of these  were distributed among 1
2 CONC 18 Bushmen by Nicolaas v. der Walt, Jacob Venter, Gerrit Kruger and  G. Meyburg. Their signatures which certify to Landdrost Bresler, the place of distribution, great grandfather of Paul Kruger has been found to read Gert Kruger H
2 CONC endriksz. See Gerrit 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kruger (e)2, son of Hendrik Bernhardus (d)2 (p. 251). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Farm or locality: 1785 Leeuwenkyl, aan de Brakke R. agter de Sneeuwberg (R.L.R. 33, p. 163). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1786 Zoutpansdrift, onder de Brakke R. (R.L.R. 34, p. 279). 1802 Brandvalleij en Rietpoort, inde 
2 CONT
2 CONT spruit van de Brakke Rivier agter de Renocerberg (G.R. 14/16, List No. 1, Item 34). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Zoutpansdrift was sold by Gerrit Kruger - or since it was a loan-farm, the opstal thereon - to 
2 CONT
2 CONT Michiel Andries van der Walt (G.R. 14/16, Etraordinaire Annotatie noopens de Leening 
2 CONT
2 CONT plaatsen, 1797). It was in 1813 in occupation of Barend Rudolf Buys (md. at that time to Helena 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothea van Wyk), the brother of Susanna Lasya Buys. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Krijger-13 WikiTree Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2020, 16:40:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT b7 Hendrik = 8/4/1725 x Kaapstad 5/5/1748 Francina CLOETE = 7/9/1732 d.v. Gerrit Cloete en Huibrecht Slabbert
2 CONT
2 CONT c2 Gerrit = 21.5.1750 x 12.11.1769 Susanna Lasya BUYS † c. 1802 d.v. Stephanus Buys en Maria Elizabeth de Vries xx 15.5.1808 Anna Sophia VENTER (wed. v. P. Snyman)
