2 CONT
2 CONT A true and perfect inventory of all the goods, chattels and wares, as well moveable as immoveable, debts, credits and personal effects of''' Robert Carr''' and deceased wife '''Gertruyda Lotriet''' which latter died at the place K
2 CONC affers Kraal in the field cornetcy of M: de Beer, Gouph, on the 31 of Dec:r 1833 and stated as follows
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Heirs of the estate
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Barend Petrus Jacobus Carr born 13 May 1818''', before the said Robert Carr’s marriage with the deceased being her son by a connection with '''Barend Botes W: z:''' and subsequently christened Carr at the wish of the deceased a
2 CONC nd said Robert Carr 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus done in the village of Beaufort on the 25 day of January 1834 in the presence of Hendrik P: Eybers and Joseph Kersner, by Robert Carr who declared that in the foregoing statement he has acted honestly and faithfully that noth
2 CONC ing has to the best of his knowledge and belief been kept back and that he is at all times ready to solemnize the same by oath, further promising and binding himself in the event of any thing belonging to this estate coming to his
2 CONC  knowledge or recollection to amplify this inventory therewith
2 CONT
2 CONT  Witnesses: H:P: Eijbers, J: Kersner
2 CONT
2 CONT  Robert Carr
2 CONT
2 CONT  In my presence: John Francis Goodwin, Agent
2 CONT
2 CONT - Inventories of the Orphan Chamber Cape Town Archives Repository, South Africa Reference no.: MOOC8/48.40 on http://databases.tanap.net/mooc/main_article.cfm?id=MOOC8%2F48.40&freesearchkey=%20Gertruyda
2 CONT
