2 CONT Bron: Wes-Kaap Argief, Kaapstad, Suid-Afrika
2 CONT
2 CONT Bron verwysing:-
2 CONT
2 CONT KAB/MG/3300 EN 3301 Liquidation and Distribution account. Robert CARR en Gertruyda LOTRIET. 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT General Liquidation Account of the Estate of Robert CARR and deceased wife Geertruyda LOTRIET, relinguished on the 31st December 1833 by the intestate death of the last mentioned in favor of her only child named Barend Petrus Jaco
2 CONC bus / born 13th May 1818 / by a connection with Barend Botes. W. Son. previously to her marriage with Robert Carr, and subsequently christened Carr, at the wish of the deceased and said Robert Carr; on behalf of which minor this E
2 CONC state was taken under administration by the late Board of Orphan Masters of this Colony and finally liquidated in this Department in manner following ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 27.28 or Pds 2.1.4 1/2 : 1834, 31 May, To, Cash, Rds 27.28 or Pds 2.1.4 1/2, paid for Advertisements in the Government Gazette, Zuid Afrikaan and South African Commercial Advertiser
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 45 or Pds 3.7.6 : 1834, 31 Aug, To, John Francis GOODWIN, Agent at Beaufort, Rds 45 or Pds 3.7.6 being the amount of Funeral Expenses paid by him for account of the Estate as per Receipt
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 102.6 or Pds 7.13.2 1/4 : 1834, 30 Sept, To, Cash, Rds 102.6 or Pds 7.13.2 1/4, in full of the Claim held by John Harris against this Estate as per Inventory
2 CONT
2 CONT [Private Note: Robert CARR passed away on 10 NOV 1834]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 94 or Pds 7.1 : 1834, 30 Novb, To, Cash, Rds 94 or Pds 7.1, paid the undermentioned in full of their Claims as above: Fredrik Schenk: Rds 50 or Pds 3.15, and John Baird: Rds 44 or Pds 3.6
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 530 or Pds 39.15 : 1835, 1 May, To, Unpaid Claims on liquidated Estates, Rds 530 or Pds 39.15, being the amount due to Charles Lennox Stretch, Land Surveyor, for the Survey of the Kafferskraal situate in the Field Cornetchy of
2 CONC  Geoph/Gouph as per Bill filed against this Estate, which is hereby carried to his credit on this account of the Ledger
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 13 or Pds 0.19.6 : 1835, 1 May, To, Expenses of Office Rds 13 or Pds 0.19.6 for Postages paid
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 4.6 or Pds 0.6.2 1/4 : 1835, 1 May, To, Cash Rds 4.6 or Pds 0.6.2 1/4, paid the Stamp Office for the undermentioned Stamps required Viz. : For the Inventory, 1 of R l and 1 of C. Stevens : Rds 1.6 or Pds 0.1.8 1/4 and Liquidat
2 CONC ion Account 1 of : Pds 3 or Pds 0.4.6
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 39.18 or Pds 2.19.0 3/4 : 1835, 1 May, To, Fees Rds 39.18 or Pds 2.19.0 3/4, being the usual charges of office in this Department Viz : For Framing Inventory : Rds 4 or Pds 0.6; For Framing Advertisements : Rds 1 or Pds 0.1.6;
2 CONC  For framing this Liquidation Account : Rds 4 or Pds 0.6; For its examination : Rds 2 or Pds 0.3; For 2 1/2 per cent on Rds 1133.30 or Pds 85.0.5 1.4 the Balance of this Account : Rds 28.18 or Pds 2.2.6 3/4
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 1105.12 or Pds 82.17.10 1/2 : 1835, 1 May, To, the interested party and heir of the deceased named in the Remises for their shares in the net balance of the Estate amounting to One Thousand One Hundred and Five Rizdollars and 
2 CONC Twelve Steviers or Eighty Two Pounds, Seventeen shillings, and 10 1/2 Viz: Robert Carr, on account of the community of Property between him and the deceased for one half : Rds 552.30 or Pds 41.8.11 1/4; Barend Petrus Jacobus Carr,
2 CONC  the only child of the deceased for the other half : Rds 552.30 or Pds 41.8.11 1/4
2 CONT
2 CONT [Private Note: Robert CARR had other children that were excluded from inheriting due to: 1. Him marrying Geertruyda LOTRIET in community of property, 2. Adopting her son Barend Petrus Jacobus BOTES, and 3. Upon her being the first
2 CONC  dying, she left a Will relinquishing her Estate to her son only.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 1960.12 or Pds 147.0.8 1/4 : TOTAL
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 1758.18 or Pds 131.17.6 3/4 : 1834, 30 April, By, John Francis GOODWIN, Agent at Beaufort, Rds 1758.18 or Pds 131.17.6 3/4, being the net proceeds of a Public Sale held for account of the Estate on the 3d Instant as per Vendu 
2 CONC Roll
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 177.4 or Pds 13.5.7 1/2 : 1834, 1 June, By, Barend Petrus Carr, Rds 177.4 or Pds 13.5.7 1/2, being the net proceeds of a Public Sale held by the Agent at Beaufort on the 3d April last for account of the said Minor as stated in
2 CONC  his letter of the 12th April last, but it appearing from a subsequent communication of the said Agent under date 6th Instant, that the property sold belongs to the Joint Estate, the amount is hereby ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 25 or Pds 1.17.6 : 1834, 31 Aug, By, John Francis Goodwin, Agent at Beaufort, Rds 25 or Pds 1.17.6, being the amount as ... to him from Sybert Neethling, in full of his debt to the Estate
2 CONT
2 CONT Pro Memoria The Place Kafferskraal belonging to this Estate is still unsold - the Grant not being yet issued by the Government - Application has been made for it and the place will be sold if it is obtained.
2 CONT
2 CONT Several debts are outstanding in favor of this Estate for the recovery of which the Agent has been written to.
2 CONT
2 CONT Master's Office, 1st of May 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed by Clarke Burton
2 CONT Master of the Supreme Court
2 CONT
2 CONT Rds 1960.12 or Rds 147.0.8 1/4 : TOTAL
2 CONT
